title: Case Manager › Filters › Search and filter both tabs
route: /manager and /manager?tab=reviews
intro: One filter bar serves both tabs. Search, level of care and payer apply to the 'Being prepared' list, the tracker and the review list. The last dropdown changes with the tab. Every filter narrows the list at once and all of them combine.
dir: TD
also: Filters are not kept in the address. They survive switching tabs, and are cleared by leaving the page or reloading.
---
start s1 "Case Manager is open"
screen sb "Filter bar\nSearch box 'Search by case ID or initials'\n'All levels of care'   'All payers'   'Any status' or 'Any review status'"

group gSearch "Search"
  input i1 "Type in 'Search by case ID or initials'"
  process p1 "Text is lowercased; dots, spaces and dashes are ignored\n'r1042', 'R-1042', 'jm' and 'J.M.' all match"
endgroup

group gLevel "Level of care"
  click c2 "Click 'All levels of care'"
  overlay o2 "Menu: 'All levels of care', 'Residential 3.5', 'IOP', 'PHP', 'Detox'"
  input i2 "Pick one"
endgroup

group gPayer "Payer"
  click c3 "Click 'All payers'"
  overlay o3 "Menu: 'All payers', 'Cardinal Health Plan', 'Summit Medicaid HMO', 'Beacon PPO', 'Harborview MA', 'Lakeshore Behavioral', 'Evergreen'"
  input i3 "Pick one"
endgroup

group gStatus "Last dropdown (depends on the tab)"
  click c4 "Active cases: click 'Any status'"
  overlay o4 "Menu: 'Any status', 'Needs action', 'Review due', 'Awaiting payer', 'On track'\nTracker only: 'Being prepared' is not filtered by it"
  click c5 "Reviews this week: click 'Any review status'"
  overlay o5 "Menu: 'Any review status', 'Needs your update', 'Drafted', 'Signed'"
  input i4 "Pick one"
endgroup

process p2 "Lists narrow at once. All filters must match (search and level and payer and status)\nThe tracker goes back to page 1"
process p3 "A dropdown that is not on its first option turns green-bordered and bold"
decision d1 "Is any filter on for this tab?"
click c6 "Click 'Clear filters' (plain button after the dropdowns)"
process p4 "Search emptied, all dropdowns back to their first option, lists full again"
process p5 "The button is not shown\n(a status filter set on the other tab does not count)"
click c7 "Press Escape, click outside, or pick again"
process p6 "Menu closes. Arrow keys move in a menu and Enter picks"
goto g1 "Continues in: Case Manager › Empty states › Nothing to show"
end e1 "List shows only the matching rows"

s1 --> sb
sb --> i1 --> p1 --> p2
sb --> c2 --> o2 --> i2 --> p2
sb --> c3 --> o3 --> i3 --> p2
sb --> c4 --> o4 --> i4
sb --> c5 --> o5 --> i4
i4 --> p2
o2 & o3 & o4 & o5 --> c7 --> p6
p2 --> p3 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| c6 --> p4 --> e1
d1 -->|No| p5 --> e1
p2 -.->|Nothing left| g1
